{# ---------- Who we are ---------- #}
<section class="cc26-wrap cc26-section cc26-about">
    <div class="cc26-about__intro">
        <div class="cc26-eyebrow">Who we are</div>
        <h2 class="cc26-h2">A buyer and seller of rare coins, gold and silver.</h2>
        <p class="cc26-lede">Cabbage Coins is a buyer and seller of rare coins, gold, and silver bars located right in the heart of beautiful Lancaster County, Pennsylvania. A few facts about Cabbage Coins:</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="cc26-facts">
        <li>
            <span class="cc26-facts__n">01</span>
            <h3>We want to be your coin dealer</h3>
            <p>We buy rare coin collections and offer free appraisals. Give us a call to discuss the collection and we'll help answer questions and give an idea around value.</p>
            <a class="cc26-textlink" href="/selltous/">Sell to us →</a>
        </li>
        <li>
            <span class="cc26-facts__n">02</span>
            <h3>Better-date coins for the astute collector</h3>
            <p>Our bread and butter are nice, encapsulated, better date coins for the astute collector. Visit our Inventory page to see the current collection for purchase.</p>
            <a class="cc26-textlink" href="/inventory/">See the inventory →</a>
        </li>
        <li>
            <span class="cc26-facts__n">03</span>
            <h3>Home in Lancaster, on the road across the mid-Atlantic</h3>
            <p>Lancaster County, PA is our home, but we're happy to travel across the mid-Atlantic to check out coin collections and scope out local coin shows for new buying opportunities.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
            <span class="cc26-facts__n">04</span>
            <h3>At the major shows</h3>
            <p>We visit most of the major national and local coin shows. If you ever see us set up as a dealer, please come by, check out our coins and say hello!</p>
            <a class="cc26-textlink" href="/coinshows/">Show schedule →</a>
        </li>
        <li>
            <span class="cc26-facts__n">05</span>
            <h3>The Cabbage Coins Podcast</h3>
            <p>Be sure to check out the YouTube podcast, where the mission is educating viewers, inspiring new collectors and elevating the quality of collections.</p>
            <a class="cc26-textlink" href="/podcast/">Watch the podcast →</a>
        </li>
        <li class="cc26-facts--story">
            <span class="cc26-facts__n">06</span>
            <h3>The story behind Cabbage Coins</h3>
            <p>It's one of the questions we're asked most often: why “Cabbage”? It began with a nickname on Instagram — and it turns out cabbage has always meant money.</p>
            <a class="cc26-textlink" href="/story/">Read the story →</a>
        </li>
    </ol>
</section>

